 "lines": [
  {
   "start": 0.5,
   "end": 4.559,
   "text": "Jesus came home to Nazareth, and taught in the synagogue.",
   "tempter": false
  },
  {
   "start": 4.959,
   "end": 8.982,
   "text": "Where did he get all this? Isn't this the carpenter? Mary's son?",
   "tempter": false
  },
  {
   "start": 9.382,
   "end": 11.35,
   "text": "And they took offense at him.",
   "tempter": false
  },
  {
   "start": 11.75,
   "end": 15.651,
   "text": "A prophet has honor everywhere, except in his own hometown.",
   "tempter": false
  },
  {
   "start": 16.151,
   "end": 20.995,
   "text": "He could do no great miracles there. And he was amazed at their unbelief.",
   "tempter": false
  },
  {
   "start": 21.595,
   "end": 28.172,
   "text": "Then he sent out the twelve, two by two. Take nothing but a staff. No bread. No bag. No money.",
   "tempter": false
  },
  {
   "start": 28.472,
   "end": 31.88,
   "text": "They went out, drove out demons, and healed the sick.",
   "tempter": false
  },
  {
   "start": 32.48,
   "end": 35.281,
   "text": "King Herod heard about it, and was afraid.",
   "tempter": false
  },
  {
   "start": 35.581,
   "end": 38.724,
   "text": "John, the man I beheaded, has come back from the dead!",
   "tempter": false
  },
  {
   "start": 39.324,
   "end": 45.937,
   "text": "Herod had put John in prison, because John told him: It is not right for you to take your brother's wife.",
   "tempter": false
  },
  {
   "start": 46.437,
   "end": 52.328,
   "text": "On Herod's birthday, there was a great feast. His wife's daughter danced, and pleased the king.",
   "tempter": false
  },
  {
   "start": 52.628,
   "end": 56.564,
   "text": "Ask me for anything, and I will give it to you. Up to half my kingdom.",
   "tempter": false
  },
  {
   "start": 56.964,
   "end": 58.333,
   "text": "What should I ask for?",
   "tempter": false
  },
  {
   "start": 58.733,
   "end": 61.241,
   "text": "The head of John the Baptist.",
   "tempter": false
  },
  {
   "start": 62.241,
   "end": 66.591,
   "text": "The king was sorry. But he would not break his oath in front of his guests.",
   "tempter": false
  },
  {
   "start": 67.191,
   "end": 71.527,
   "text": "That night, in the prison, the voice in the wilderness went silent.",
   "tempter": false
  },
  {
   "start": 72.727,
   "end": 76.838,
   "text": "His disciples came, took his body, and laid it in a tomb.",
   "tempter": false
  },
  {
   "start": 77.638,
   "end": 80.901,
   "text": "Follow for part ten.",
   "tempter": false
  }
 ]
}